                    # mirror and through each restart's WAL replay. On the first boot measured, a Degraded child failed the
                    # root sync at once, and the root's retry backoff then outlasted the image pull. So not-ready pods read
                    # as Progressing, and the wave simply waits. Reconciled False stays Degraded: the operator could not
                    # build the pods, so waiting will not help.
                    # Cost: a Prometheus that can never start reads Progressing rather than Degraded. Before this, root retried
                    # and re-read the newest commit each time. Now it waits with no retry, so a fix to
